sequenceDiagram
    title Invariant — WatcherChannel is single-writer (OS callback) / single-reader (REPL at boundary)

    participant FS as Filesystem
    participant OS as OS Notify Callback Thread
    participant Channel as WatcherChannel
    participant REPL as REPL Thread
    participant Sched as Compilation Scheduler

    Note over Channel: invariant: OS thread is sole writer.<br/>REPL thread is sole reader.<br/>reads happen only at prompt boundary

    FS ->> OS: file change event
    OS ->> Channel: push(FileChange{path, mtime})
    FS ->> OS: another file change
    OS ->> Channel: push(FileChange{path2, mtime})

    Note over OS,Channel: writes are serialized within the OS callback thread.<br/>OS may push at any time relative to REPL

    Note over REPL: REPL is mid-input — does not read channel
    Note over REPL: prompt boundary reached (between input and submit)

    REPL ->> Channel: drain()
    Channel -->> REPL: [FileChange1, FileChange2]

    REPL ->> REPL: dedup vs known content hash<br/>(suppress self-writes from cache regeneration)

    REPL ->> Sched: ReRegisterRequest for affected modules

    Note over Channel: between drains, channel buffers events.<br/>REPL never polls inside an input-handling step
